{
  "requirement": "Marks an agent request that has begun collecting node contents. Further node inputs can be added before awaiting the answer.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct NodePhase;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`NodePhase` is a marker type. It has two obligations: (1) a request that has begun collecting node contents is in this phase, and (2) more node inputs can be added in this phase before the answer is awaited.\n\nThe marked test is `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]`. It builds a request with `ctx.ask::<Answer>().context(..)`. It then chains `.contents_of_current_node().contents_of_successors(7).contents_of_current_node().into_future()`.\n\n- **Entering the phase:** In `procedure.rs`, `contents_of_current_node` and `contents_of_successors` return `Ask<.., NodePhase>`, so the first node input moves the request into this phase.\n- **Adding further node inputs:** The second and third calls are made on the `NodePhase` value. Both input kinds are added, and one kind is repeated.\n- **Awaiting the answer from this phase:** `into_future()` is called on the `NodePhase` request. The test awaits it and asserts `answer.n == 7`.\n- **Effect of the added inputs:** The test asserts the agent received the contents in insertion order: 1, 3, 2, 3, 1. It also asserts the graph reads and the recorded dependencies. A phase that dropped or reordered later inputs would fail these checks.\n\nThe `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` test checks that the public export inventory matches the book. That covers the `pub struct NodePhase;` declaration being exported.\n\nNo obligation is left untested. The phase is a compile-time marker, and the chained calls compile only if the typed transitions exist.",
  "references": "909f09d5168c839a764d052216fd8a81d52222d7dce5a9a991746bb17ad69803",
